# Solution: React Hooks Order Bug in ResultsCharts

## Problem
React threw a 'Rendered more hooks than during the previous render' error in ResultsCharts. This was caused by calling hooks (useState, useMemo, useEffect) after early returns for missing data.

## Error Messages
- Warning: React has detected a change in the order of Hooks called by ResultsCharts.
- Uncaught Error: Rendered more hooks than during the previous render.

## Root Cause
- Early returns before all hooks were called, causing React to see a different number/order of hooks between renders.

## Solution Steps
- Move all hooks (useState, useMemo, useEffect) to the top of the component, before any early returns.
- Only do conditional returns after all hooks have been called.

## Code Example

**Wrong (causes error):**
```tsx
function MyComponent(props) {
  if (!props.data) return <div>No data</div>;
  const [state, setState] = useState(0); // This hook is not always called!
  // ...
}
```

**Right (always safe):**
```tsx
function MyComponent(props) {
  const [state, setState] = useState(0); // Always called
  if (!props.data) return <div>No data</div>;
  // ...
}
```

## Verification
- The error is gone and the component renders correctly.

## Future Improvements
- Always call hooks at the top of every React function component, before any conditional logic or returns.
